OL,3,GNEWSADecisions before woman's sepsis
OL,4,Adeath 'indefensible'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman who died in hospital after
OL,7,Fcontracting sepsis could have survived
OL,8,Fif "indefensible" decisions had not
OL,9,Fbeen made, an inquest was told.
OL,11,FCoroner Darren Stewart concluded
OL,12,Ffailures by West Suffolk Hospital
OL,13,F"directly contributed" to the death of
OL,14,F28-year-old Hannah West.
OL,16,FAt the end of Friday's hearing, he took
OL,17,Fthe rarely seen step of reporting two
OL,18,Fdoctors involved in her care to the
OL,19,FGeneral Medical Council, before
OL,20,Frecording a narrative conclusion.
